    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **269 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp08Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date default for owner creation. When an owner is created without a registration date, it now defaults to today's date and is returned in the owner response as `registrationDate` in ISO format (`YYYY-MM-DD`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `registrationDate` field (`format: date`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and Jackson serializes it as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it between `Owner` and `OwnerDto` by name.\n\n3. **`controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it isn't already set.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb; the others are kept consistent. Existing `data.sql` inserts list columns explicitly, so the nullable column doesn't affect seed data.",
